  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The lead was theirs from the first inning until the ninth inning arrived and Pittsburgh took it back.",
    "what_this_means": "Gelof carried them early. 3-for-3, a home run, two RBI. The kind of night that should have been enough. They led by as much as four runs. The bullpen collapsed after the sixth. Harris gave up two in the seventh. Alvarado added one in the ninth. Perkins had done his job at the start: five innings, three runs, six strikeouts. The relief arms couldn't hold a deficit that narrow. Twelve runners left on base across 12 RISP situations. They converted two of them into runs. In a game decided by one run, two conversions out of twelve is not enough. The last inning was empty. Two more chances, two more left there. This is a team that holds leads and then stops holding them. The margin disappears not in the big moments but in the middle ones, the innings where you're supposed to add on and don't.",
    "what_to_watch": "Civale goes tonight against Ashcraft, who owns a 3.30 ERA and will come with the Buccos looking to make it two straight.",
